event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":190,"item_id":"rs_057be2f9e040f565016aca3581dbf081959b0455474584c975","output_index":0,"summary_index":1,"text":"**Refining function names**\n\nI’m considering renaming the function from formData to a global parseForm for clarity. The local formData captures the request setting for selectedPriority and the URL filter. I'm also mulling over whether the detailPage, an alias for projectPage, shadows the global one. For redirects, using an augmented string at the taskFilter function might complicate things. Instead, I plan to straightforwardly edit four blocks around 500 characters each to maintain unique contexts for the operations."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":191,"item_id":"rs_057be2f9e040f565016aca3581dbf081959b0455474584c975","output_index":0,"summary_index":1,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Refining function names**\n\nI’m considering renaming the function from formData to a global parseForm for clarity. The local formData captures the request setting for selectedPriority and the URL filter. I'm also mulling over whether the detailPage, an alias for projectPage, shadows the global one. For redirects, using an augmented string at the taskFilter function might complicate things. Instead, I plan to straightforwardly edit four blocks around 500 characters each to maintain unique contexts for the operations."}}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":192,"output_index":0,"item":{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_057be2f9e040f565016aca3581dbf081959b0455474584c975","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Exploring function complexities**\n\nI'm thinking about the filter argument for location and whether I need to make repeated replacements using edit. It’s possible I could change the formData call globally, but that adds unwanted complexity. It's probably better to generate an edit through asynchronous tool invocations since loops can't call that way. I need to ensure my context remains unique across the data lines, which seems complicated. A bash script might work, but explicit rewrites could be a challenge too."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Refining function names**\n\nI’m considering renaming the function from formData to a global parseForm for clarity. The local formData captures the request setting for selectedPriority and the URL filter. I'm also mulling over whether the detailPage, an alias for projectPage, shadows the global one. For redirects, using an augmented string at the taskFilter function might complicate things. Instead, I plan to straightforwardly edit four blocks around 500 characters each to maintain unique contexts for the operations."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqyjWNUIVHk3rHEUomzS1yvgRu6ibPygLW9EnZ1_LdPgM1Nph2uJasket74Ky9Tb917z7g01O6MngrDeCpyogNEj0lpICy0KEanLwS9l8pHMllhxYe8wy9ql_X4F7rfEg9A-ya4FSL8xf-K8U5d9b9-ULYTz9ZeBollG1Z-KpmSa2Ahvf60bySSV_1WzTQDirPvoncl6rpmEjfRqcHCM8-VVT8RbTH9RNieOx8Ygf-aqnlcYt66oyD4cgyiQHtnnXN3dSH4X3e8CueZ1zv3H8KCRDYvMSxxKWjjL3EaqO34OxhQ-abpLV2Qt34HubCnqVruXdjFr3xY4NBylyquoQCRjoaao-imcptlVvo-IgvULUk3ObVJMHRxBqppNl7fMUhgXUpdH9DtvKM6BfLxodOdQAM5avHl5336MjTc_AEwY9bClzURcQrGI1MWg4vEjd0pLkSYwfr7BvroiRQRGU6xurZDNz42y-kIv59oC-wEaG54fTbC4nni2zsC1MQEbhO-UN4XceYRqe8ZNsErWNDgSKKHkf_wZmDmaCMkivUuC29buTt0xSd5UJpC8nYl9Tfc-y18RXx7AAmqYZIYrsea4weXuuRlnyG8DARBcM4bUTtVKNL3tKuQOhQwA4ZM5bd_AEaxmV6o7z1SPF3xFBbov0b_